{"cluster_id": "C-3008", "topic": "replaceFile routes a mutable-file destination to", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B035-089"], "canonical_claim": "`replaceFile` routes a mutable-file destination to `recorded_mutable`, and the temporary name must itself satisfy `isMutablePerPartFile` as `<mutable>.tmp`; otherwise standalone autocommit can republish a one-file manifest and clobber the part.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-transactions", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#second-pass-gap-fill"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3009", "topic": "On CA, an uncommitted contract", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-021", "B035-090"], "canonical_claim": "On CA, an uncommitted INSERT publishes a ref whose blobs remain GC-reachable but is governed-invisible through `txn_version.txt`; ROLLBACK removes the ref and makes the blobs GC-eligible, while `getLastModified` on a ref-less in-flight part must use the in-flight overlay. An uncommitted INSERT inside an open transaction still publishes a CAS ref whose blobs stay GC-reachable via a `WriteSession` pin until the ref lands; the part is logically invisible via its `txn_version.txt` creation CSN. ROLLBACK removes the ref, after which the blobs become GC-eligible.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L605-L611", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-transactions", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#second-pass-gap-fill"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3010", "topic": "A multi-part disk transaction contract", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-023", "B035-091"], "canonical_claim": "A multi-part disk transaction uses a per-part `std::map<{table_uuid, part_name}, PartStaging>` and can span a deferred `tmp_merge_X \u2192 X` rename plus `txn_version.txt` rewrites for covered source parts; CA publishes parts one at a time, with MVCC visibility providing logical atomicity and GC reclaiming crash-orphaned refs. A transactional multi-part commit is not filesystem-atomic on CAS: MVCC visibility is gated by the per-part CSN/TID in `txn_version.txt`, not by disk-op atomicity, so CAS may publish parts one at a time; a crash mid-commit leaves some refs published and some not, and orphan refs are GC-reclaimed exactly as any uncommitted-then-abandoned build (B122).", "issue_ids": ["B122"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L656-L664", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-transactions", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#second-pass-gap-fill"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3011", "topic": "Gc::runRegularRound invokes Gc::drainCompletedRemoving immediately after lease", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B036-009"], "canonical_claim": "`Gc::runRegularRound` invokes `Gc::drainCompletedRemoving` immediately after lease acquisition and before heartbeat work, DEFER, the hot stream LIST, the authoritative catalog cut, plan construction, or fold.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaGcDestructiveGateCore_RESULTS.md#code-correspondence"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3012", "topic": "The completed-removing drain uses CasRefCatalog::deleteCompletedRemovingAtSnapshot for", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B036-008", "B036-011"], "canonical_claim": "The completed-removing drain uses `CasRefCatalog::deleteCompletedRemovingAtSnapshot` for an exact catalog CAS, resolves its outcome, and rescans until no eligible row remains; it performs no physical cleanup.; Catalog-only pre-fold erasure of a proved `Removing` lifecycle row is independent of the later physical destructive gate and must not be suppressed by unrelated later-round anomalies or carried holds.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaGcDestructiveGateCore_RESULTS.md#code-correspondence", "docs/superpowers/models/CaGcDestructiveGateCore_RESULTS.md#suppressed-physical-work-with-exact-erasure"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3013", "topic": "Shard reclaim must wait until the", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B036-036"], "canonical_claim": "Shard reclaim must wait until the shard journal is fully folded, including its tombstone, before token-guarded `deleteExact`; deleting earlier can orphan a folded edge and leak the target blob.", "issue_ids": ["D1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaGcShardIncarnationCore_RESULTS.md#conclusions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3014", "topic": "The writer cleanup lifecycle precommits ownership", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B037-121"], "canonical_claim": "The writer cleanup lifecycle precommits ownership, atomically replaces the precommit with the committed owner on promote under the current epoch, and cleans failed builds in resolve-grant \u2192 remove \u2192 retire order.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/README.md#group-ref-table"]}
